#: scripts/scenario_39_escape.lua:1041
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid "Starfighter"
msgstr "Starfighter"

#: scripts/scenario_39_escape.lua:1047
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"Starfighters are single to 3 person small ships. These are most commonly "
"used as light firepower roles.\n"
"They are common in larger groups, and need a close by station or support "
"ship, as they lack long time life support.\n"
"It's rare to see starfighters with more then one shield section.\n"
"\n"
"One of the most well known starfighters is the X-Wing.\n"
"\n"
"Starfighters come in 3 subclasses:\n"
"* Interceptors: Fast, low on firepower, high on manouverability\n"
"* Gunship: Equipped with more weapons, but trades in manouverability because "
"of it.\n"
"* Bomber: Slowest of all starfighters, but pack a large punch in a small "
"package. Usually come without any lasers, but the largers bombers have been "
"known to deliver nukes."
msgstr "Starfighters are single to 3 person small ships. These are most commonly used as light firepower roles.\nThey are common in larger groups, and need a close by station or support ship, as they lack long time life support.\nIt's rare to see starfighters with more then one shield section.\n\nOne of the most well known starfighters is the X-Wing.\n\nStarfighters come in 3 subclasses:\n* Interceptors: Fast, low on firepower, high on manouverability\n* Gunship: Equipped with more weapons, but trades in manouverability because of it.\n* Bomber: Slowest of all starfighters, but pack a large punch in a small package. Usually come without any lasers, but the largers bombers have been known to deliver nukes."

#: scripts/scenario_39_escape.lua:1051
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid "Frigate"
msgstr "Frigate"

#: scripts/scenario_39_escape.lua:1057 scripts/scenario_39_escape.lua:1124
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"Frigates are one size up from starfighters. They require a crew from 3 to 20 "
"people.\n"
"Think, Firefly, millennium falcon, slave I (Boba fett's ship).\n"
"\n"
"They generally have 2 or more shield sections, but hardly ever more than 4.\n"
"\n"
"This class of ships is normally not fitted with jump or warp drives. But in "
"some cases ships are modified to include these, or for certain roles it is "
"built in.\n"
"\n"
"They are divided in 3 different sub-classes:\n"
"* Cruiser: Weaponized frigates, focused on combat. These come in various "
"roles.\n"
"* Light transport: Small transports, like transporting up to 50 soldiers in "
"spartan conditions or a few diplomats in luxury. Depending on the role it "
"can have some weaponry.\n"
"* Support: Support types come in many varieties. They are simply a frigate "
"hull fitted with whatever was needed. Anything from mine-layers to science "
"vessels."
msgstr "Frigates are one size up from starfighters. They require a crew from 3 to 20 people.\nThink, Firefly, millennium falcon, slave I (Boba fett's ship).\n\nThey generally have 2 or more shield sections, but hardly ever more than 4.\n\nThis class of ships is normally not fitted with jump or warp drives. But in some cases ships are modified to include these, or for certain roles it is built in.\n\nThey are divided in 3 different sub-classes:\n* Cruiser: Weaponized frigates, focused on combat. These come in various roles.\n* Light transport: Small transports, like transporting up to 50 soldiers in spartan conditions or a few diplomats in luxury. Depending on the role it can have some weaponry.\n* Support: Support types come in many varieties. They are simply a frigate hull fitted with whatever was needed. Anything from mine-layers to science vessels."

#: scripts/scenario_39_escape.lua:1061
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid "Corvette"
msgstr "Corvette"

#: scripts/scenario_39_escape.lua:1067
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"Corvettes are the common large ships. Larger then a frigate, smaller then a "
"dreadnaught.\n"
"They generally have 4 or more shield sections. Run with a crew of 20 to "
"250.\n"
"This class generally has jumpdrives or warpdrives. But lack the "
"maneuverability that is seen in frigates.\n"
"\n"
"They come in 3 different subclasses:\n"
"* Destroyer: Combat oriented ships. No science, no transport. Just death in "
"a large package.\n"
"* Support: Large scale support roles. Drone carriers fall in this category, "
"as well as mobile repair centers.\n"
"* Freighter: Large scale transport ships. Most common here are the jump "
"freighters, using specialized jumpdrives to cross large distances with large "
"amounts of cargo."
msgstr "Corvettes are the common large ships. Larger then a frigate, smaller then a dreadnaught.\nThey generally have 4 or more shield sections. Run with a crew of 20 to 250.\nThis class generally has jumpdrives or warpdrives. But lack the maneuverability that is seen in frigates.\n\nThey come in 3 different subclasses:\n* Destroyer: Combat oriented ships. No science, no transport. Just death in a large package.\n* Support: Large scale support roles. Drone carriers fall in this category, as well as mobile repair centres.\n* Freighter: Large scale transport ships. Most common here are the jump freighters, using specialised jumpdrives to cross large distances with large amounts of cargo."

#: scripts/scenario_39_escape.lua:1071
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid "Dreadnought"
msgstr "Dreadnought"

#: scripts/scenario_39_escape.lua:1077
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"Dreadnoughts are the largest ships.\n"
"They are so large and uncommon that every type is pretty much their own "
"subclass.\n"
"They usually come with 6 or more shield sections, require a crew of 250+ to "
"operate.\n"
"\n"
"Think: Stardestroyer."
msgstr "Dreadnoughts are the largest ships.\nThey are so large and uncommon that every type is pretty much their own subclass.\nThey usually come with 6 or more shield sections, require a crew of 250+ to operate.\n\nThink: Stardestroyer."

